{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1541516","title":"Prokaryotes from the AnSBBR subjected to different co-substrates. Raw sequence reads","description":"Conventional wastewater treatment plants (WWTPs) are often ineffective at removing micropollutants (MPs), such as pharmaceuticals and artificial sweeteners, raising environmental concerns. This study evaluated the physicochemical characteristics of raw and treated domestic wastewater from a full-scale aerobic ABC WWTP, and assessed a laboratory-scale Anaerobic Sequencing Batch Biofilm Reactor (AnSBBR) operated with six co-substrates (sucrose, ethanol, lactose, cheese whey, glucose, and glycerin) with respect to the removal of caffeine (CAF), ibuprofen (IBU), diclofenac (DCF), cyclamate (CYC), and sucralose (SUC).","center":"University of Sao Paulo","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2026/10/08 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN64067478","Metagenome or environmental sample from Prokaryotes from the AnSBBR subjected to different co-substrates.","non_environmental",null,"2025-05-02",2025,"BR","São Paulo",3449319,"São Carlos","verified",-22.001,-47.93,"Brazil: Sao Carlos, SP","AnSBBR reactor",null,null,null,"laboratory or culture material"]],"run_cols":["accession","sample","experiment","assay","strategy","source","layout","platform","instrument","bases","spots","release_date","download_url"],"runs":[["SRR41184188","SAMN64067478","SRX35693669","Amplicon","AMPLICON","METAGENOMIC","PAIRED","ILLUMINA","NextSeq 2000",50186797,83558,"2026-10-14","https://sra-downloadb.be-md.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sos12/sra-pub-zq-1216/SRR041/41184/SRR41184188/SRR41184188.lite.1"],["SRR41184189","SAMN64067478","SRX35693668","Amplicon","AMPLICON","METAGENOMIC","PAIRED","ILLUMINA","NextSeq 